  "notes": "Cash basis city. Governmental from Total column of the cash-basis governmental funds statement (p4: General + Bond). Grants and donations 70,233 printed below the Excess line as Other Financing Sources; recorded as a receipt with outside_printed_total (donations/contributions). Business-type (Water, Sewer) from proprietary statement p6 (Total column, accrual); depreciation included as an expense; bond proceeds 921,562 in business_type.debt_proceeds; net position used as measure. No printed single total for business-type receipts/disbursements, so computed. Several printed totals are off by 1 (see report_discrepancies). Balance sheet is the government-wide Statement of Net Position Total (memo only) column p1; debt (notes and bonds payable) not split by due date. Detail: General Fund recorded from the budget-and-actual schedule (p8) which gives the budget; the combining schedule of General sub-funds (p11: General, Sales Tax, Library, Auditorium, Park, Streets, Keno) was not entered to avoid double counting (it has 7 columns; totals tie to the same fund totals; Public buildings 57,514 and culture 541,002 = 598,516 on p8). Proprietary budget schedule p10 is budgetary basis (differs from p6 statement, negative capital improvements as printed). Hidden-transfer cross-check: no transfers printed. Ending cash 49,168,707 is the printed total fund balance / total assets the statement rolls forward (p3); it includes special assessments receivable 5,337, so cash alone is 49,163,370. Read pages 1-11 of 11."
